course: dictionary
lesson: 3204
title: Engineer: a maker and a designer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An engineer is a person who designs and builds things such as bridges, roads, machines and computers, using science and maths. Engineer can also be a verb: to engineer something means to design and build it, or to arrange it cleverly.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Engineers invented the microchip, which put many tiny parts onto a small piece of silicon.» Invented and microchip tell you the engineers were making something new and clever, so an engineer is someone who makes and designs things.
explain: «Power lines and substations are for engineers only: never climb a pylon.» The words for engineers only and never climb tell you that engineers are trained people who work safely on dangerous machines. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check it fits.
fact: An engineer designs and builds machines, bridges, roads, buildings and computers.
fact: Engineers use science and maths to solve problems and make things work.
fact: «Colossus» was built at Bletchley Park by engineer Tommy Flowers, and it was one of the first electronic computers.
fact: Engineers copied the bumps on the flippers of humpback whales to help design fan and turbine blades.
fact: To engineer something can also mean to arrange it cleverly, sometimes secretly.
exercise: «Colossus, built at Bletchley Park in 1943 to 1944 by engineer Tommy Flowers, was one of the first electronic computers.» What is an engineer? | A person who writes books about whales | A person who sells food at a market | A person who drives buses | *A person who designs and builds machines and other things
exercise: «Power lines and substations are for engineers only: never climb a pylon.» Why should children never climb a pylon? | Because pylons are painted bright yellow | Because pylons are too short to climb | *Because only trained people should work safely on power lines | Because pylons are made of soft wood
exercise: «A doctor in London mapped where people fell ill, and an engineer built huge sewers after a summer called the Great Stink.» Which word tells you what the engineer did? | huge | summer | Stink | *built
test: Which best describes an engineer? | A person who grows vegetables on a farm | A person who sells tickets on a train | A person who only paints pictures | *A person who designs and builds things, using science and maths
test: Which sentence uses engineer as a verb, a doing word? | The engineer checked the bridge for cracks | The engineers wore yellow hats | The bridge had a plaque with an engineer's name | *The team engineered a way to keep the bridge up
exam: Which job title means someone who designs computer programs? | *software engineer | civil pylon | Great Stink inspector | microchip maker
